olet","dish/damien-pignolet"],["Daube","dish/daube"],["Demi-glace","dish/demi-glace"],["Duxelles","dish/duxelles"],["Espagnole sauce","dish/espagnole-sauce"],["Fin gras du Mézenc","dish/fin-gras-du-mezenc"],["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"],["Foie gras","dish/foie-gras"],["Foin de Crau","dish/foin-de-crau"],["Fraisier","dish/fraisier"],["French onion soup","dish/french-onion-soup"],["French restaurant","dish/french-restaurant"],["Fricassee","dish/fricassee"],["Garbure","dish/garbure"],["Gâteau Basque","dish/gateau-basque"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Hollandaise sauce","dish/hollandaise-sauce"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/b0/Landj%C3%A4ger.jpg/500px-Landj%C3%A4ger.jpg","w":500,"h":469,"by":"MarkusHagenlocher","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landj%C3%A4ger.jpg"}},"dish/new-york-roll":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/new-york-roll","n":"New York roll","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Cuisine of the Mid-Atlantic United States","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["The New York roll or cromboloni (a mix of croissant and bomboloni) is a viennoiserie that gained popularity in the 2020s through social media. Videos on TikTok that featured the roll gained hundred of thousands of views. It is made from circular croissant dough, and filled with pastry cream and topped with a chocolate ganache. It originated from the United States. It was originally called The Suprême. It can be enhanced with many different flavors such as chocolate, pistachio, and caramel."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-new-york-roll"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_roll"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cuisine of the Mid-Atlantic United States","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-mid-atlantic-united-states"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/c/cd/New_York_Roll.jpg/500px-New_York_Roll.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"LittleT889","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_York_Roll.jpg"}},"dish/nisholda":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/nisholda","n":"Nisholda","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Nisholda, also spelled as nishallo, nishaldo, or nisholda is a sweet dish that resembles white jam, only thicker. It is popular in Afghan, Iranian, Tajik, and Uzbek cuisines. Nisholda is also a traditional dish among the Bukharan (Central Asian, Samarkand) Jews."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-nisholda"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nisholda"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Afghan cuisine","cuisine/afghan-cuisine"],["Iranian cuisine","cuisine/iranian-cuisine"],["Tajik cuisine","cuisine/tajik-cuisine"],["Uzbek cuisine","cuisine/uzbek-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Citric acid","ingredient/citric-acid"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Afghan Culture Unveiled","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"afghancultureunveiled.com","note":"Afghan-American Humaira Ghilzai's blog on Afghan food and culture.","url":"https://www.afghancultureunveiled.com/humaira-ghilzai/afghancooking/2013/01/our-aushak-recipe-in-print-food52.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Afghan Cooks","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"afghancooks.com","note":"Recipe blog dedicated to traditional Afghan dishes.","url":"https://afghancooks.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Unicorns in the Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"unicornsinthekitchen.com","note":"Iranian-born Shadi HasanzadeNemati's blog with a large Persian recipe section.","url":"https://www.unicornsinthekitchen.com/persian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Afghan cuisine","links":[["Falooda","dish/falooda"],["Kabuli pulao","dish/kabuli-pulao"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Thali","dish/thali"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/3/36/Nisholda_produced_in_Russia.jpg/500px-Nisholda_produced_in_Russia.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"ИП Кадиров Х.Р.","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nisholda_produced_in_Russia.jpg"}},"ingredient/tamarind-juice":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/tamarind-juice","n":"Tamarind juice","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Tamarind juice (also known as tamarind water) is a drink or ingredient made by extracting the sweet-sour pulp of tamarind (Tamarindus indica) into water. The tamarind tree is native to tropical Africa and has long been cultivated across tropical and subtropical regions, where its pulp is widely used in beverages as well as foods. Tamarind juice can be consumed as a beverage appreciated for its fresh sour taste, or used for culinary purposes as a sour flavouring agent. In addition to traditional uses, tamarind is used in some modern cocktails and non-alcoholic mixed drinks for its tart flavour."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-tamarind-juice"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamarind_juice"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Pad thai","dish/pad-thai"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bean sprouts","ingredient/bean-sprouts"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut sugar","ingredient/coconut-sugar"],["Dried shrimp","ingredient/dried-shrimp"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Fish sauce","ingredient/fish-sauce"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Jaggery","ingredient/jaggery"],["Lime (fruit)","ingredient/lime-fruit"],["Mung bean sprout","ingredient/mung-bean-sprout"],["Peanut","ingredient/peanut"],["Rice noodles","ingredient/rice-noodles"